  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-31T17:21:02.096Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It would be very useful for external tools generating dolly paths to be able to receive the current absolute position and rotation of the user (or all of them in multi streaming mode?)\n\ncurrently the only way to do that is to make the user add a point at the beginning or end of the path, trigger a export, parse that and then regenerate the path\n\nvery clunky\n\nthe player (head?) position and rotation would also work, the current available options do not account for teleportation and would only allow calculating relative to spawn location, which is also not always in the same place\n\nso having that in absolute values would help a lot \n\nfoudn another canny for that: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/additional-parameters-for-reading-current-players-position",
